{
  "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
  "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Karen R. King",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KING: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Hague Convention provides that a court is not bound to return a child once the grave risk exception is met."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: The way you just framed the inquiry, Ms. King, is like, well, first, we decide whether there's a grave risk, and then we see whether there's anything that we can do about it. But is it -- is that necessarily the right way to frame the -- the --the issue? I mean, how do you decide really whether there's a grave risk without thinking about ameliorative measures at -- at that stage? I mean, is this really a two-step inquiry, or should we think about ameliorative measures in order to determine whether there's a grave risk?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I have a -- sort of a threshold problem in understanding this statute and the way the parties and the Solicitor General have interpreted it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. King",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KING: Well, we would suggest that after a grave risks finding, courts have discretion to deny the petition for return or to grant it subject to ameliorative measures. But consistent with the convention, any"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Liu",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LIU: About three and a half years."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Min",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is precisely our argument, that connected to the grave risk inquiry, one must show that the child cannot be protected or cannot be treated in the home country. It's not sufficient to show, well, the child can get medical treatment in the United States; we don't have to worry about what's available in the other country. They must engage in some sort of analysis of what is possible and appropriate in the home country before --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you disagree with any of those?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Davies case, which occurred the year before this case in the Second Circuit, the district court denied the return to French St. Martin after ameliorative measures and undertakings were proposed. The -- on remand, the Second Circuit did not -- on -- on appeal, the Second Circuit did not remand for failure -- failure to consider the full plan -- panoply of ameliorative measures, for failure to consider all theoretical ameliorative measures. They simply affirmed stating the -- the district court considered the record put forth before them, considered available ameliorative measures, and agreed that the child should not be returned."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How would you describe the consideration in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Blondin amicus",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0003-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "again, in the Blondin amicus brief, criticize the grave risk process, which required expert testimony, and said that it would result to delays and prolonging cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "what mechanism is there for a court to do that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. King",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0003-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 82,
        "start": 82
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the exception exists for a reason. And this is the first case where a mother has proven the grave risk exception by the exceedingly high evidentiary standard in this country, by clear and convincing evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6779fe44e8632209c327ae74ac88c5dc5cee939ba4fb9afebd2e8324e1fa2121",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6779fe44e863-0003-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 83,
        "start": 83
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "note that that finding was never even appealed. It stands to this day, all of those findings of horrific violence, of the character failings of Mr. Saada, and of the harm, psychological and physical harm, to the young child in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
